  "cues": [
   [
    0.117,
    "But electrons do not jump from glucose to oxygen directly."
   ],
   [
    4.089,
    "Glucose is taken apart in a series of steps, and at many of them, the first helper is an enzyme called a dehydrogenase."
   ],
   [
    12.018,
    "The dehydrogenase takes two hydrogens from the fuel molecule."
   ],
   [
    16.042,
    "That means two protons and two electrons."
   ],
   [
    19.141,
    "It hands the two electrons, and one proton, to a molecule called NAD\u207a."
   ],
   [
    25.091,
    "The other proton is simply released into the surrounding solution."
   ],
   [
    29.154,
    "The fuel loses electrons, so it is oxidized."
   ],
   [
    32.409,
    "NAD\u207a gains electrons, so it is reduced."
   ],
   [
    36.133,
    "That makes NAD\u207a the oxidizing agent."
   ],
   [
    39.896,
    "The slide draws a generic fuel molecule, not glucose, because glucose goes through several of these steps."
   ],
   [
    46.667,
    "We will meet them in lessons four and five."
   ]
  ]
