   [
    0.104,
    "Now compare two ways of making water."
   ],
   [
    2.682,
    "In the first, hydrogen and half an oxygen react in one step."
   ],
   [
    7.096,
    "The energy drops all at once and leaves as heat and light, an explosion."
   ],
   [
    12.422,
    "Respiration makes the same water, from two protons, two electrons and half an oxygen."
   ],
   [
    18.568,
    "But the electrons from NADH go down a chain of carriers."
   ],
   [
    22.695,
    "Each carrier hands them to a slightly lower one, so the free energy falls in small steps, like a staircase."
   ],
   [
    29.922,
    "At each stage, a part of the energy is captured to make A T P, and the rest leaves as heat."
   ],
   [
